  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/keepalive.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/agent-errors.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/translation/*.test.ts

Reasoning turned off, sent the way each model takes it: thinkingOffOf,
thinkingOffAsTaken and withoutThinkingOff in anthropic.go, thinkingBackOn in
wire_effort.go, and the refusal words (alwaysThinks, refusesThinkingOff,
thinkingOffRefused in anthropic.go; mandatoryReasoning, effortLevelsNamed,
noneQuoted in gateway.go) with the retry at the lowest level in gateway.go.
Their tests reuse cases from thinking_off_test.go, sub2api_think_off_test.go
and gateway_test.go. The Codex catalog's default reasoning level follows
ModelDefault in internal/codexcat/codexcat.go and NearestEffort in
internal/catalog/catalog.go:

  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/refusals.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/refusals.test.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/translated.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/codex-model-catalog.ts
  packages/server/src/server/daemon-e2e/api-endpoint-gateway.e2e.test.ts

The request-format choice (chooseRequestFormat) follows magpie's usable and
MessagesFirst (internal/gateway/gateway.go, internal/provider/provider.go);
which names are the same model (sameModel in internal/provider/group.go) and
the closest ids a model not found names (Closest in internal/provider/closest.go,
unknownModel in internal/gateway/unknown_model.go) are ported from magpie too,
and so is sending Codex's memory and auto-review calls to the model of its last
turn (internal/gateway/codex_memory.go, callKind in codex_backend.go):

  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/routing.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/routing.test.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/gateway/codex-side-calls.ts

Request-format auto-detection (each format's base URL, the model asked, the
smallest request) follows magpie's internal/provider/detect.go and test.go:

  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/upstream-detect.ts

Who owns the modelPicker in Claude Code's settings.json (the user's is left
alone; magpie's own is rewritten, or dropped when it has no rows) follows
writePicker and dropPicker in magpie's internal/agent/claude.go:

  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/claude-settings-patch.ts

What Claude Code is told about an endpoint model it doesn't know (the [1m]
mark, CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS, CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS,
CLAUDE_CODE_MODEL_CAPABILITIES, and leaving a value the user set alone)
follows claude1M, claudeWindow, claudeOutput, claudeCaps and
claudeCapabilities in magpie's internal/agent/claude.go; how a model is
looked up in the models.dev catalog (the bare id, the value most providers
give) follows bareID, found, mostGiven, mostListed and window in magpie's
internal/catalog/catalog.go:

  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/claude-model-hints.ts
  packages/server/src/server/api-endpoints/model-facts.ts

